cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite this software only with the exact revision and retained evidence used."
title: "Etzio: An Evidence-Native Engine for Authorized Vulnerability Research"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wahnich
    given-names: Daniel
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-08-01
url: "https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/etzio"
repository-code: "https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/etzio"
abstract: >-
  Etzio is an evidence-native engine for authorized vulnerability research. A candidate
  becomes a finding only when a separately authorized verifier reproduces a material effect
  from retained bytes and the kernel accepts the receipt. The current execution surface is
  repository-owned deterministic fixtures; no live-target, execution, external-provider, or
  finding capability is established. See LICENSE.md — this repository is public source under a
  proprietary license, not an open-source grant.
keywords:
  - authorized vulnerability research
  - evidence-native systems
  - independent reproduction
  - content-addressed evidence
  - deterministic replay
  - RFC 9162
